Attribution
===========

ultraopen ports the design of Claude Code's "Workflow" tool and its "ultracode" effort mode to
opencode.

Portions of the tool description and the workflow-authoring reference are adapted from Anthropic's
Claude Code. They are kept close to the original deliberately: the wording of the opt-in gate, the
pipeline-versus-parallel decision rule and the pattern catalogue is behaviourally load-bearing — a
model reads it and writes different code as a result — so paraphrasing it would change what the
tool does. Treat that text as part of the implementation rather than as documentation.

Adaptations are limited to what opencode actually does:
  - `Workflow({...})` -> `workflow({...})`, the opencode tool id
  - "the Agent tool" -> "the task tool"
  - the asynchronous task-id contract rewritten as blocking, because opencode exposes no
    background-job route to a plugin
